3. ROWS SKIPPED / PARTIALLY APPLIED — with reason
================================================================
- a#49, b#9, b#44(number half), ACCEPTED "Number format: 500 000 / 1 579 589":
  NOT applied in the columns. scripts/check-column-translation.mjs cannot parse space-grouped
  thousands — NUMBER_THOUSAND_STYLE.ru = 'dot' and the grouped-token regexes only accept [.,],
  so «1 579 589» tokenises as 1, 579, 589. Proven empirically: converting 010 to space thousands
  produced `numbers FAIL missing from translation (11): 1000000x2, 1570000x8, 1579589` and
  `summary FAIL 17/18`. Per the WO ("prefer the form the checker accepts"), the existing dot form
  stays in all 18 columns. In the guidance pack (not checker-covered) the supervisor's format WAS
  applied: «добилась решения первой инстанции на 1,57 млн TWD».
  -> Supervisor action if the space form is wanted: teach the checker a space/NBSP thousands group
     for ru (and the other space-grouping locales).
- a#53 (ISO dates «2026-05-29» / «2026-07-01» in 003 §body): NOT applied, checker-blocked.
  The checker's month lexicon has января…декабря but is MISSING «мая», so «29 мая 2026 г.» loses the
  month token and yields `numbers FAIL missing from translation (1): 5`. («1 июля 2026 г.» parses
  fine.) Rather than mix one Russian and one ISO date in the same sentence, both were left ISO.
  -> Supervisor action: add `мая: 5` to the month lexicon, then this row is a one-line change.
- a#18 (percent-encoded Hangul related-reading link in 005): skipped per ACCEPTED-ru (R1, already
  remapped). Verified: `hangul PASS`, no Hangul outside `url` in any ru column.
- b#25 (Invest Taiwan `lang=jpn`): left as-is per the WO's known-checker-constraint note (link parity;
  supervisor fixes centrally).
- b#1 (byline «**Адвокат Wei Tseng (曾雋崴)**» -> «Wei Tseng (曾雋崴), адвокат на Тайване»): not applied
  per ACCEPTED-ru — «адвокат» is common gender and the supervisor chose to keep the byline; only verbs
  and participles around it were made feminine. Same for a#3's first-person line in 008.
- a#66 (retitle 008 to «Трудовое право Тайваня: когда выплачивается выходное пособие (資遣費)»):
  only the «??» -> «?» half applied. The English source title IS a question ("Taiwan Labor Law: Is
  Severance Pay Hard to Get in Taiwan?"), and the WO's hard rule is to keep the meaning of the English
  source, so the question form was preserved instead of replacing it with a statement.
- Rows about /ko/ links, "Korean-speaking lawyer" labels, Hangul `url:` frontmatter: skipped per
  ACCEPTED-ru (already done mechanically in R1). New labels re-read and left as they are.

